      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents of originalism argue that the Constitution should be understood based on the ** original public meaning** of the text at the time it was adopted. This approach believes the Constitution is a fixed, authoritative text, and its meaning should not change with the political views of the present.\n\nThe main support is that this method **restrains judicial power** by demanding that judges adhere to the will of the framers and the people who approved the law. This, in the view of originalists, promotes **predictability and limits bias** in the law, making the Constitution consistently applied for all time.",
